  "query_preview": "../Sunday Through Mid Week/...Beginning the latter \nhalf of the weekend will be a return to high pressure for much of \nthe eastern gulf, with a trough exiting to the south of Haida \nGwaii. For winds, northwesterlies along the western coast south of\nCape Edgecumbe are expected to increase to at least 20 knots as \nthe trough drops south and the high pressure builds. Aloft, a \nweak, dirty ridge with some energy working eastward along the \nnorthern gulf will keep a general cloudiness with a nonzero \npossibility of rain, particularly for the northeast gulf coast and\nIcy Strait over to Juneau. Furthermore, timing regarding these \nshowers certainly display a high degree of uncertainty. Chances \nfor right now are around 20% particularly around Sunday night and \nthrough Monday, with highest chances along west facing mountains.\n\n\nTransitioning into the midweek, a stronger system moves into the \nAnchorage area, with a portion of the storm spilling into the \nYakutat Area. Not expecting any impactful rainfall totals at this \ntime, with a majority of the moisture directed towards Prince \nWilliam Sound and westward.",
